  "id": "Compound::DB04845 - Gene::7280",
  "verbalization": "Ixabepilone is linked to Tubb2a through a series of molecular interactions that involve microtubule inhibition and binding to tubulin-related proteins. The evidence suggests that Ixabepilone, through its inclusion in microtubule inhibition, indirectly binds to Tubb2a via Eribulin, which itself binds to Tubb2a. This pathway is supported by the shared lowest common ancestor of Ixabepilone and Eribulin, both of which are classified under the \"Tubulin Binding Agent\" category. The presence of \"Cyclic Ether\" as a common ancestor further reinforces the connection between Ixabepilone and Eribulin, suggesting a shared structural or functional role in tubulin interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights a mechanism by which Ixabepilone may influence Tubb2a through its interaction with Eribulin, which in turn binds to Tubb2a. This relationship is further supported by the inclusion of Ixabepilone in microtubule inhibition, indicating a broader role in tubulin-related processes.",
